# Git Workflow

## Branch Strategy

```
main              ← Production-ready, always deployable
  ↑
develop           ← Integration branch, staging
  ↑
feature/*         ← New features
fix/*             ← Bug fixes
refactor/*        ← Code improvements
docs/*            ← Documentation changes
```

### Branch Naming

```bash
feature/add-multi-currency-support
feature/streaming-websocket-endpoint
fix/pdf-parsing-amount-extraction
refactor/agent-factory-pattern
docs/api-endpoint-documentation
```

### Workflow

```bash
# Start new feature
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/add-batch-reconciliation

# Work on feature (commit frequently)
git add .
git commit -m "feat(graph): add batch reconciliation node"

# Push and create PR
git push -u origin feature/add-batch-reconciliation
# Create PR → develop

# After PR approval and merge
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git branch -d feature/add-batch-reconciliation
```

## Commit Message Format

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description>

[optional body - explain WHY, not WHAT]

[optional footer - breaking changes, issue refs]
```

### Types

| Type | When to use |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature or capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Code change that neither fixes nor adds feature |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `chore` | Build, CI, dependency updates |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |

### Scopes (project-specific)

| Scope | Covers |
|-------|--------|
| `api` | FastAPI endpoints, request/response models |
| `graph` | LangGraph state, nodes, graph composition |
| `agent` | Agent factories, LLM configuration |
| `prompt` | System prompts, templates |
| `config` | Settings, environment, configuration |
| `deps` | Dependency changes |

### Examples

```bash
feat(graph): add validation node before reconciliation
fix(agent): handle Claude timeout with graceful fallback
refactor(api): extract request validation into Pydantic models
docs(prompt): update system prompt with ambiguity handling rules
test(graph): add unit tests for node_reconcile state transitions
perf(agent): implement response streaming with chunked output
chore(deps): update langgraph to 0.3.x
```

## Pre-commit Checklist

Before every commit:

- [ ] Type hints on all new/modified functions
- [ ] Docstrings on all public functions
- [ ] No hardcoded paths or API keys
- [ ] Logging instead of print()
- [ ] Tests pass (when test suite exists)
- [ ] No `.env` or sensitive files staged

## Versioning

Use [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/):

```
MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH

0.1.0  → Initial working prototype
0.2.0  → Added new endpoint or feature
0.2.1  → Bug fix
1.0.0  → Production-ready release
```

Tag releases:
```bash
git tag -a v0.1.0 -m "feat: initial reconciliation pipeline"
git push origin v0.1.0
```
